# Generated protobuf is COMMITTED, not ignored (ADR-0022). `docker compose up`
# on a clean clone must build the catena image with no `buf`, no reachable
# buf.build, and no `make` step first -- and Task 7 puts catena in the default
# `up`. `make check` asserts that regenerating produces no diff, which is what
# keeps a committed artefact honest.
#
# Byte-compiled stubs are still ignored, below, with the rest of __pycache__.

# Go
/bin/
*.test

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.uv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Environment and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key

# Corpus text NEVER enters this repository (ADR-0014). All of /data/ is ignored, with no
# exceptions and no negation patterns — downloads, intermediate conversions, and staged
# records all live here and none of them are committable.
/data/

# Acquisition manifests and fingerprints live in /corpora/ and contain no corpus text.
# Per-corpus adapters live in services/catena/src/catena/acquire/corpora/. Both are committed.

# Local model cache
/models/

# OS
.DS_Store
